# NET-1 pass 1: GameNetworkingSockets behind INetTransport (Desert/Net) + the connect handshake with the cook hash.
# The network half runs outside the editor (no window, no device): Tools/DesertNetProbe in server and client mode
# on loopback, every process with the GNS simulator at 75 ms one-way send lag (150 ms RTT) and 2 % send loss,
# messages of 1100 bytes (about one packet each, so the loss hits messages and the reliable lane retransmits).
# Logs go to <scratch>/NET-1/logs/{server,clientA,clientB,clientC}.log; the player below runs only the editor part.
#   DesertNetProbe --server --port 27020 --cook-hash 0xC0FFEE --clients 2 --messages 1000 --lag-ms 75 --loss 2
#   DesertNetProbe --client --connect 127.0.0.1:27020 --cook-hash 0xC0FFEE --name A --messages 1000 --lag-ms 75 --loss 2
#   DesertNetProbe --client --connect 127.0.0.1:27020 --cook-hash 0xC0FFEE --name B --messages 1000 --lag-ms 75 --loss 2
#   DesertNetProbe --client --connect 127.0.0.1:27020 --cook-hash 0xBADBAD --name C --messages 1000 --lag-ms 75 --loss 2
# Тогда [net1a_handshake] server.log: "accepted" for A and B; for each "received 1000/1000 in order, 0 lost";
#   clientA.log and clientB.log: "received 1000/1000 in order, 0 lost", the server summary for their own 1000,
#   RTT 140-170 ms, GNS lifetime stats with dropped packets > 0; server.log and clientC.log: "cook hash mismatch";
#   exit codes A 0, B 0, C 2 (refused), server 0.
# The editor is untouched by this pass, but the tree must still build and open the WP world.
Проект Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/WP_Protocol.desce
Дано state
Тогда 0_wp_protocol WP_Protocol opens as in dev: landscape, town, sky; no crash or error dialog; no load refusal in editor.log
